<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79213" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰρειά</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>(v. infr.), <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			22.1421.124
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			1455.11
		</span></i>, etc. ; but <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρεά</span></b>  ib.<i><span class="en">
			1425.246
		</span></i> ; 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραύα</span></b>  (q.v.) ; 
			Dor.
		 *<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρᾱά</span></b> 
		(implied in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐπάραος</span>) ; Old 
			Ion.
		 *<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρηή</span></b> 
		(implied in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλιπάρηος, μιλτοπάρηος</span>,
		and the adjectival <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρή-ιον</span>)
			:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cheek</i>,
			used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always in pl. (sg. being supplied by the 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρήϊον</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.35
			</span></i>,al.; of an eagle, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.153
			</span></i> : also Trag., in pl., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				783
			</span></i> (lyr.) : in sg., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				401
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1239
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				280
			</span></i> (lyr.) : rare in Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				270e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.4.3
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cheekpiece</i> of a helmet, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Hom.</u>
				31.11
			</span></i> (s. v. l.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1421.124
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1455.11
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς πρῴρας τὰ
				ἑκατέρωθεν</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.89
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς παρειά</span>
			<i>earth-flush</i>, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμώνη ἡ φοινικῆ</span>
			, cj. in Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.176
			</span></i>. (Perh. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά, οὖς</span>,
			lit. <i>beside the ear.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>